3. FORUM SELECTION AND JURISDICTION CLAUSE:
In the event of a breach of Section 1 or Section 2 of this Amendment—including 
but not limited to unauthorized data mining, text mining, or AI ingestion—the 
violating party, user, corporate directors, and agents hereby explicitly agree, 
consent, and submit to be summoned to, and be subject to the exclusive 
jurisdiction of, the Federal Court of Canada (sitting in Ottawa, Toronto, or 
any other designated Canadian judicial registry). 

The violating party waives any and all objections to venue or personal 
jurisdiction in the Federal Court of Canada, including the defense of forum 
non conveniens, and agrees that all legal disputes, claims, and enforcement 
actions resulting from unauthorized data scraping shall be litigated exclusively 
within the Federal Court of Canada under Canadian federal law.

4. LIQUIDATED DAMAGES:
Any entity found in breach of this agreement agrees to pay the Copyright Holder 
statutory damages under the Copyright Act (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-42) or a minimum 
